{
  "chapter.66AA476364390298.title": "08 • XNet: Channels and Control",
  "task.05BDC66A8C76EF21.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.5D482EA2D901A236.title": "Start here: XNet",
  "quest.5D482EA2D901A236.quest_subtitle": "Start Here",
  "quest.5D482EA2D901A236.quest_desc": [
    "XNet combines item, fluid, energy and control routing through a compact cable network. A Controller holds channels; each channel defines a job and connector settings determine how each endpoint participates. It suits factories that need central configuration without writing a program.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/xnet.png width:330 height:150 align:center}",
    "",
    "&b&lChoose a branch&r",
    "• First Channel",
    "• Processing & Stock",
    "• Fluids, Power & Control",
    "• Routing & Projects",
    "",
    "Your route: powered controller -> connected inventories -> item channel -> filters and faces -> fluids and energy -> multiple machines -> routers and a complete processing cell.",
    "",
    "&eStart with the first equipment milestone, then follow the branch you need."
  ],
  "task.5CDC097DE21253A4.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.2FFB17ED8EB75DC7.title": "Map legend & completion rules",
  "quest.2FFB17ED8EB75DC7.quest_subtitle": "Reference",
  "quest.2FFB17ED8EB75DC7.quest_desc": [
    "Follow a branch that solves your next problem. Equipment icons lead to concrete inventory milestones; the book card is a reference, and a large diamond marks a workshop project.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the setup before crafting. Item milestones detect your inventory without consuming items. Their practical checkmarks are optional reminders; final workshop projects require a practical confirmation. An item in your bag does not prove that a machine is configured. Existing equipment counts: do not rebuild a working system just for this map.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "JEI shows this pack's current recipes. Branches explain how the systems connect. Optional side projects are independent of the main route; no casino win is required."
  ],
  "task.7CB3D5CEC1E4BF66.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.0A1C039E0485CD09.title": "Build the control point",
  "quest.0A1C039E0485CD09.quest_subtitle": "First Channel",
  "quest.0A1C039E0485CD09.quest_desc": [
    "The Controller is where the network's channels are configured. It needs power and reachable connectors to do useful work.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Craft a Controller, compatible network cable and connectors. Supply FE, connect two chests, and open the Controller to check that the endpoints are listed.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep your first network in one loaded area and use one cable color. Different colored networks are intentionally separated."
  ],
  "task.123BD0C32E7D4E5C.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.436CDBF32678D44B.title": "Cable is the road; connectors are the doors",
  "quest.436CDBF32678D44B.quest_subtitle": "First Channel",
  "quest.436CDBF32678D44B.quest_desc": [
    "A cable run links the network, while connectors expose adjacent blocks to the Controller. A cable merely passing a machine is not enough.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect where each connector touches its chest. Rename or otherwise identify the endpoints in your layout. Disconnect one temporarily and observe which entry disappears.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Leave physical access to machine faces. A neat cable bundle is less helpful if it prevents you reaching the input side you need."
  ],
  "task.14F0BC4FBC74AE80.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3616E99D31390D00.title": "One channel, one job",
  "quest.3616E99D31390D00.quest_subtitle": "First Channel",
  "quest.3616E99D31390D00.quest_desc": [
    "Channels describe the resource and transfer behavior. Starting with one job makes every setting easier to understand.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Create an item channel. Configure one chest connection to extract and the other to insert, enable the channel, and transfer a few cobblestone.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "CONTROLLER SCREEN: Choose an unused channel and make it an Item channel. In the connector list for that channel, set the source to Extract and the destination to Insert. Both rows must be enabled. Put eight iron ingots in the source and observe them arrive.",
    "",
    "TWO DIFFERENT COLORS: Cable colors separate physical networks. Item-channel filters/priorities control a route within one controller. Changing a cable color is not a substitute for configuring the source and destination rows.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Check both the channel and endpoint settings when nothing moves. Listing an inventory in the Controller does not automatically assign a transfer job."
  ],
  "task.7316724EE981BF9C.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.303408939651539D.title": "Filter before connecting valuables",
  "quest.303408939651539D.quest_subtitle": "First Channel",
  "quest.303408939651539D.quest_desc": [
    "Filters limit which items a connection handles. An unrestricted extract can move everything in a mixed chest.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Set a cobblestone filter at the extracting endpoint. Mix cobblestone and dirt in the source and confirm dirt stays behind. Inspect the available matching options before using tagged or component-bearing items.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use a small test stack of enchanted or named items when learning matching behavior; never assume all variants are interchangeable."
  ],
  "task.0849CD24473EDA10.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.72F0D9534A22C619.title": "Make machine sides explicit",
  "quest.72F0D9534A22C619.quest_subtitle": "Processing & Stock",
  "quest.72F0D9534A22C619.quest_desc": [
    "Machine inventories are exposed according to their own side configuration. XNet cannot insert through a face that the machine refuses.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Replace the destination chest with a powered processing machine. Set its input side, inspect the connector settings, and feed one known recipe ingredient.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "FURNACE EXERCISE: A vanilla furnace wants ore through its top, fuel through a horizontal side, and output removed below. With ordinary connectors, place connections on the appropriate physical faces. An advanced connector can provide more face-control options.",
    "",
    "SPLIT THE JOB: Use separate item channels or deliberate filters for raw material, fuel and finished ingots. If your output rule has no filter and points at an input inventory, it can take material back before the furnace uses it.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "First prove the machine runs when supplied by hand. That separates recipe or power problems from transport problems.",
    "",
    "{image:customatm:textures/quests/xnet.png width:330 height:150 align:center}"
  ],
  "task.5D349D0543C235B6.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.62982FA9DE6FC808.title": "Remove the finished product",
  "quest.62982FA9DE6FC808.quest_subtitle": "Processing & Stock",
  "quest.62982FA9DE6FC808.quest_desc": [
    "Supplying ingredients without extracting output eventually stops production. The return route is a distinct job worth checking on its own.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Add an output connection/channel as needed. Configure extraction from the machine's output side into a result chest, then process several batches.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep input and output filters distinct. Broad rules attached to the same inventory can circulate ingredients endlessly."
  ],
  "task.1B673BD2875631F8.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.06AF177A21F52931.title": "Stock levels and priorities",
  "quest.06AF177A21F52931.quest_subtitle": "Processing & Stock",
  "quest.06AF177A21F52931.quest_desc": [
    "Limits keep a machine supplied without hoarding the entire network's ingredients. Priority decides which eligible destination should be served first.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Inspect the item connector's available count and priority controls. Give a primary machine a small stock target, add a second destination, and observe how a limited supply is shared.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Test behavior at the target stock level and with a full destination. Priority is a routing preference, not an ingredient generator."
  ],
  "task.2170AA0B29AEC008.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3BCB6A25C89CC654.title": "Give fluids their own channel",
  "quest.3BCB6A25C89CC654.quest_subtitle": "Fluids, Power & Control",
  "quest.3BCB6A25C89CC654.quest_desc": [
    "Fluid movement follows tank capacity and exposed faces rather than item slots. Separate channels make the intended path clear.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Connect two tanks, add a fluid channel and transfer water from one to the other. Set the relevant fluid filter and demonstrate that a full destination safely stops transfer.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Confirm that the destination accepts the fluid. Similar-looking liquids from different mods can have different registry identifiers."
  ],
  "task.1FE417BA0B1163EF.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.0BF831C0D9936965.title": "Distribute FE deliberately",
  "quest.0BF831C0D9936965.quest_subtitle": "Fluids, Power & Control",
  "quest.0BF831C0D9936965.quest_desc": [
    "Energy channels let the same network power multiple machines, but the Controller and source must remain able to operate.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Add an energy channel from a charged buffer to a machine. Observe the buffer and machine energy levels while processing. Keep a dependable supply to the Controller itself.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A factory can fail because it lacks total generation even when every channel is configured correctly. Watch energy over several cycles, not just one moment."
  ],
  "task.17C40C829FCBAF2A.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.436B2B31FA242413.title": "Use control signals",
  "quest.436B2B31FA242413.quest_subtitle": "Fluids, Power & Control",
  "quest.436B2B31FA242413.quest_desc": [
    "Redstone and channel conditions can stop production when a switch is off or a condition is not met.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the installed XNet manual's channel and logic pages. Add one visible control condition to your test line and demonstrate enabled and disabled states.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Add control after ordinary routing works. Record what the condition means so a future stopped machine is easy to diagnose."
  ],
  "task.19F1E30EE975DA7E.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.52DEC77FE782E2E1.title": "When advanced connectors help",
  "quest.52DEC77FE782E2E1.quest_subtitle": "Processing & Stock",
  "quest.52DEC77FE782E2E1.quest_desc": [
    "Advanced connectors offer additional capability and higher transfer performance. They are useful where an ordinary connection is the measured bottleneck.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Compare normal and advanced connector tooltips and settings in JEI/the Controller. Upgrade one busy endpoint and observe whether transfer behavior improves.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A faster connector cannot accelerate a slow machine recipe or compensate for inadequate FE. Upgrade the constrained part of the system."
  ],
  "task.7C766A75ED78BFF9.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.54D90CCEB8C0FA5E.title": "Separate neighboring networks",
  "quest.54D90CCEB8C0FA5E.quest_subtitle": "Routing & Projects",
  "quest.54D90CCEB8C0FA5E.quest_desc": [
    "Cable colors provide physical separation between systems that happen to pass near one another.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build a second short cable run in another color beside your test network. Confirm it does not silently become part of the first Controller's endpoint list.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Choose a consistent color convention for production areas, then label it. Color alone does not describe the job of each channel."
  ],
  "task.5914A64F84140815.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.4EBD6A891A6AB73F.title": "Routers connect larger systems",
  "quest.4EBD6A891A6AB73F.quest_subtitle": "Routing & Projects",
  "quest.4EBD6A891A6AB73F.quest_desc": [
    "A Router lets controllers exchange published channels through a routing network. It is an expansion tool after local channels work.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Read the installed router manual page. Make two small working local networks, publish a test channel through the routing setup and connect the receiving controller according to the router interface.",
    "",
    "&6&lWorkshop notes&r",
    "TWO WORKING NETWORKS: Each controller should already move an item locally. Publish the intended channel with a clear name, attach the controller-side network to the router arrangement, then connect the matching published channel through routing.",
    "",
    "TEST THE BOUNDARY: Move one known stack across the two systems. If each local channel works but the cross-system transfer does not, inspect the published names, router connections and routing cable network before changing machine-side settings.",
    "",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Use routing cables where required by the router setup. Do not treat a router as an ordinary longer cable and assume every channel is shared."
  ],
  "task.06DDB259DDD4980D.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.67CCD513FA0890BB.title": "Wireless routing",
  "quest.67CCD513FA0890BB.quest_subtitle": "Routing & Projects",
  "quest.67CCD513FA0890BB.quest_desc": [
    "Wireless routers extend routing between separated areas using an antenna arrangement. Antenna construction determines the supported range.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Consult the wireless-router and antenna pages, build the described antenna above the router, and test a short link before increasing distance.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Both ends still need functioning local routing, power and loaded chunks. Wireless reach does not automatically keep a remote factory loaded."
  ],
  "task.6A8050C6379BBC1D.title": "I understand this reference",
  "quest.36820FE443D6DA6D.title": "Trace a stalled transfer",
  "quest.36820FE443D6DA6D.quest_subtitle": "Routing & Projects",
  "quest.36820FE443D6DA6D.quest_desc": [
    "The Controller centralizes diagnosis: endpoint visibility, channel state, direction, filters, limits and conditions can all stop a transfer.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Choose a stalled step and trace one item from source to destination. Verify source contents, extraction, enabled channel, insertion, machine side and free space. Inspect power lastingly, not only at idle.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Temporarily use two chests to isolate the network from a complicated machine. Restore the machine only after the simpler route works."
  ],
  "task.7C8B23F8654DFC68.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.6B6E4AE6FBEDF860.title": "Project: one-cable processing cell",
  "quest.6B6E4AE6FBEDF860.quest_subtitle": "Routing & Projects",
  "quest.6B6E4AE6FBEDF860.quest_desc": [
    "A useful XNet cell combines distinct jobs while keeping them understandable in the Controller.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Build a machine cell with FE supply, filtered ingredient input, output extraction and an on/off condition. Add a second machine without breaking the first, then name the channels and document their purpose.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep a small buffer and a visible output while learning. Expand to a base-wide router network only after each local cell has predictable behavior."
  ],
  "task.79635D51FE66C512.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.695FB70F6E75B9A2.title": "Two endpoints, one controller",
  "quest.695FB70F6E75B9A2.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • First Channel",
  "quest.695FB70F6E75B9A2.quest_desc": [
    "Connectors expose adjacent inventories to the controller. A cable running past a chest without the appropriate connector does not give the channel an endpoint.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Connect two chests with two matching-color connectors and a short cable run to a powered controller. Open its interface and locate both connectors before configuring any channels.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Name endpoints Source and Results where the interface allows. Those names make later channel setup easier to verify."
  ],
  "task.4539F0B99AF3158F.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.2B6E5949ED1C0568.title": "Give the furnace a recipe",
  "quest.2B6E5949ED1C0568.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Processing & Stock",
  "quest.2B6E5949ED1C0568.quest_desc": [
    "Item movement is only useful if the receiving face accepts the intended slot. The top of a vanilla furnace is a convenient demonstration of sided inventory access.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Configure a raw-iron extraction rule from a source chest and insert through the furnace top. Start with eight raw iron and verify its input slot fills while fuel and output slots remain distinct.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If the source drains but the furnace is empty, stop and locate the items before changing the filter or adding more."
  ],
  "task.00624ED1670165D2.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.1029EC5F43F79CC0.title": "Fuel uses its own route",
  "quest.1029EC5F43F79CC0.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Processing & Stock",
  "quest.1029EC5F43F79CC0.quest_desc": [
    "Fuel should enter the furnace fuel slot, not compete with ore for the top input. A separate channel makes this distinction visible.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Add a coal-only route through a horizontal furnace face. Keep its stocking amount small, run the raw-input route, and confirm the furnace processes one batch.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "The output route should remove the product from below. Test each face individually before combining all three channels."
  ],
  "task.76E35506989F1280.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3DFC04D54BF238DE.title": "Upgrade a measured bottleneck",
  "quest.3DFC04D54BF238DE.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Processing & Stock",
  "quest.3DFC04D54BF238DE.quest_desc": [
    "Advanced connectors offer capabilities beyond a basic connection. Use them when a real side-access or transfer requirement warrants the upgrade.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Compare the basic and advanced connector controls in the installed manual/UI. Upgrade one endpoint, change only the needed setting and repeat your previous successful transfer test.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "A faster connection cannot fix a full destination, disabled controller, or item filter that excludes the product."
  ],
  "task.68A03E49515360A7.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.4C2BFDE663C48BDC.title": "Separate the routing network",
  "quest.4C2BFDE663C48BDC.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Routing & Projects",
  "quest.4C2BFDE663C48BDC.quest_desc": [
    "Routing cable links routing infrastructure rather than acting as an ordinary colored item network. Keep the two roles visually distinct.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Prepare a small routing cable run for two already-working local controller networks. Publish clearly named channels and check the router sees the intended pair before sending a test stack.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "If no published channel appears, inspect the controller/router attachment and channel name. More ordinary cable does not publish a channel."
  ],
  "task.45A8159D24584A43.title": "I completed the setup and observed the result",
  "quest.3372DE492FA50F82.title": "Full chest, controlled recovery",
  "quest.3372DE492FA50F82.quest_subtitle": "Workshop • Routing & Projects",
  "quest.3372DE492FA50F82.quest_desc": [
    "Automation must handle a full destination without silently moving products somewhere unintended. A controlled stop is a normal operating state.",
    "",
    "&b&lGet it working&r",
    "Fill a disposable output chest with cheap blocks, run a tiny furnace batch and watch the finished item wait. Clear space, verify extraction resumes and confirm it still uses the intended destination.",
    "",
    "&e&lTip&r",
    "Keep an obvious off switch for the controller or upstream supply. Diagnose one channel at a time."
  ]
}
